WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:05.470
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
on Doctor Who we got one of our First Game

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.490
of Thrones Crossovers since Series 5 when
Ser Jorah guest starred. We also got to meet

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.990
Danny Pink, the new character at Coal Hill
School. So just like my episode 1 video I’ll

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:14.650
do my top 5 moments, then post as many of
the references I could find and then my review.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.730
If you’re just finding me for the first
time I’m also doing a weekly Series 8 giveaway.

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:20.619
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment. I’ll explain at the

00:00:20.619 --> 00:00:21.619
end of the video.

00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:24.789
Careful for spoilers in case you haven’t
seen the episode. But here are my top 5 moments.

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:27.560
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.009
Number 5 - Coal Hill School is a major destination
for series 8

00:00:31.009 --> 00:00:34.850
I’m totally loving the meta thing that’s
going on with Capaldi and Coal Hill School.

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:39.610
He and Moffat are weaving in a lot of first
doctor things. Coal Hill School is one of

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.289
those. The school itself has been featured
a lot in the series. But I got such a first

00:00:44.289 --> 00:00:46.199
doctor vibe from this episode.

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:51.739
Add to that, the second official episode of
the first doctor’s run was “The Daleks”.

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:56.829
So you see, Moffat is intentionally making
us think about that first season of Doctor

00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:01.290
Who. I’m wondering if that’s going to
tie in with Missy and the arc of series 8?

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.590
There are things from a lot of classic doctor’s
runs so it’s not only about the first doctor.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:06.050
Don’t limit yourself to looking for those
references.

00:01:06.050 --> 00:01:11.080
But anytime we revisit something for the first
time in series 8, think about the first time

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:12.970
that character or monster was featured.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.390
There will be some new monsters this series
though. It’s not all about revisiting classics.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:20.250
Even if the Doctor is “Correcting Mistakes
of the Past.”

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.470
Number 4 - The Doctor Returns with Coffee

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:26.680
I love how it felt like Clara bumping into
him in the closet happened directly after

00:01:26.680 --> 00:01:30.610
they walked off screen in episode 1. Like
he told her to wait a sec, she turned around

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.860
and 3 weeks later he’s back with her order.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:39.990
What does he do during those, “I’ll be
right back moments?”

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:44.330
It was a great callback to Amelia Pond in
the series 5 opener. Moffat used that be right

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:50.080
back joke a lot during Matt Smith’s run,
so I’m not expecting to see it a lot this

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.080
year.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.360
I think he’ll gently work in more 11th Doctor
Moments. But not all the time.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:57.740
There’s always the danger of just making
a new doctor a complete amalgam of the old

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:03.000
ones but so far I’ve been really happy with
the ratio of new peter capaldi things to old

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.330
doctor references.

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.590
Number 3 - Welcome To Heaven

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:10.130
Missy is back. Isn’t it funny how Journey
Blue woke up on the tardis at the beginning

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.610
and then woke up in Heaven at the end of the
episode.

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:20.250
Notice the transitions both times. It’s
like the Doctor Materalized the TARDIS around

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:23.920
her, usually that’s how he saves someone
when he doesn’t pull them in the front door.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.550
This makes me think more about the Missy TARDIS
/ Rani theories.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:33.780
If Missy were a personification of a TARDIS
she’d have the same abilities as a tardis

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:36.890
to materialize something around Journey Blue,
and if she’s the Rani she could have her

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:39.260
own TARDIS and heaven could just be a room
inside that.

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:42.980
I’ve also seen a lot of Black Guardian theories.
But for all intents and purposes, think of

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:48.100
Missy as being someone who has the same technology
as the Time Lords or at least the same abilities

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.620
if she’s not from Gallifrey. Although I’m
still convinced that the Missy plot will tie

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.720
in with the finding Gallifrey plot.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:57.720
She seems like she’s collecting the dead,
or at least zapping away their souls at the

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.130
final moment of death. Because we did see
the android body impaled on the clocktower.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:06.550
So she didn’t beam his body away. Maybe
it’s their life force she’s after?

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:10.940
There were already a lot of gravesite spoilers
as it relates to cyber conversion. I’m not

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.270
going to repeat them, just because most of
you probably haven’t seen the pictures.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:15.510
If you do want to comment on missy cybermen
theories just use spoiler tags in the comments.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:17.980
Number 2 - Welcome Danny Pink

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.880
So many things going on here. You have all
the coal hill school first doctor callbacks

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:26.020
to barbara wright and ian chesterton, then
on top of that he was also confirmed as an

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:27.349
official new companion.

00:03:27.349 --> 00:03:31.120
I don’t know why the BBC waited so long
in confirming that Pink would be turning into

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.720
a companion, because a lot of the news earlier
this year pretty much said ‘new companion’

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:40.310
I love that he’s ex-military and pretty
clearly suffers from post traumatic stress.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:44.099
Sherlock Watson anyone. This makes me feel
like once he becomes a full time companion,

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:46.459
the Wholock references will just go off the
charts.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:51.501
I’ll talk more about the Capaldi Danny Pink
vibe in my review. But Wholock is already

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:53.720
happening and it’s name is Danny Pink.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.440
The thing that really surprised me was his
relationship with Clara. I didn’t think

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.270
they’d be shipping them so quickly. But
I love it already. And the way they jumped

00:04:00.270 --> 00:04:05.319
forward and backward in time when Clara was
trying to get Danny to ask her out. She’s

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:07.440
the boss of everybody.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:13.170
Couple of red flags to watch out for. Did
you catch when Clara joked about Danny crying?

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.970
That was a pretty clear reference to his Post
Traumatic Stress. Like Watson before he met

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:22.300
Sherlock in series 1. The PTSD will probably
play role in Danny’s TARDIS episodes.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:27.439
The Doctor isn’t a huge fan of soldiers
either, so that’s not good.

00:04:27.439 --> 00:04:31.159
Then at the end, when Danny said “I thought
you had a rule against soldiers.” That’s

00:04:31.159 --> 00:04:36.770
a callback to Matt Smith being the crazy warrior
the Silence were trying to kill and to the

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.680
Darkness Capaldi’s exhibiting.

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.050
Which leads me to my Number 1 moment - The
Doctor Is A Good Dalek

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:49.789
This has been a recurring theme. The Doctor
is just as bad as the Dalek’s sometimes.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:54.210
The line, you would make a good dalek was
also from Christopher Eccleston’s run. Nice

00:04:54.210 --> 00:04:55.639
9th Doctor Callback.

00:04:55.639 --> 00:05:01.389
He was also the Post Tramatic Stress Doctor
too, one who had trouble dealing with the

00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:03.569
psychological after effects of the Time War.

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:07.249
So he and Danny Pink have a lot in common
in that sense. Expect Series 8 to play on

00:05:07.249 --> 00:05:09.499
that idea when they finally start traveling
together.

00:05:09.499 --> 00:05:13.309
Thematically the episode was really about
the Doctor testing the belief that beings

00:05:13.309 --> 00:05:18.860
cannot change their true nature. Daleks are
evil personified and can never be good. And

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:22.370
I think the Doctor hates a lot of the Darkness
inside himself, so he’s wondering if it’s

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.870
possible for him to change his nature.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:28.001
The whole “Clara, Am I A good Man” was
a perfect story runner to mirror the dalek

00:05:28.001 --> 00:05:29.419
turned good story.

00:05:29.419 --> 00:05:32.809
But let me know what you’re favorite moment
was and do you think the Doctor would make

00:05:32.809 --> 00:05:33.809
a good Dalek?

00:05:33.809 --> 00:05:37.150
It’s pretty clear the episode wants us to
think yes, he would make a fine Dalek.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:40.699
So here’s a couple of the bigger references
and easter eggs I saw in the episode. If there

00:05:40.699 --> 00:05:43.690
were some you saw please add them in the comments.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:48.620
First was the Empire Strikes Back asteroid
chase. Then the soldier’s name was Journey

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:54.689
Blue, as in Tardis Blue, traveling on the
Aristotle, I took that to be another subtle

00:05:54.689 --> 00:06:04.819
reference to Fires of Pompeii. The crazy military
base reminded me of Torchwood from the David

00:06:04.819 --> 00:06:05.819
Tennant years.

00:06:05.819 --> 00:06:12.059
Then there was Doloros Edd from Game of Thrones.
Someone tell Jon Snow the Wall has another

00:06:12.059 --> 00:06:18.319
deserter. Daleks being the theme of the episode
was also a nice reference to the first doctor’s

00:06:18.319 --> 00:06:22.460
second episode “The Daleks”. There were
a lot more references to that episode too,

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:28.119
like when the Doctor referenced seeing Skaro
for the first time.

00:06:28.119 --> 00:06:31.550
Them flying down the waterslide tubes into
the goo made me think of Beast Below. Which

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.749
was the second episode of Matt Smith’s first
year.

00:06:33.749 --> 00:06:40.210
Shrinking themselves down to go inside the
Dalek reminded me of Fantastic Voyage. Clara

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:46.629
meeting Danny Pink was a lot like Ian Chesterton
and Barbara Wright. Their costumes were even

00:06:46.629 --> 00:06:48.520
very similar to Ian and Barbara’s original
costumes.

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:53.069
There’s all the Watson, Sherlock references
in Danny Pink’s background and Capaldi’s

00:06:53.069 --> 00:06:59.310
personality. That’s only going to get better
in future episodes. Pink even had his collar

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:04.789
turned up like Sherlock. Capaldi is Sherlock,
but you get the idea.

00:07:04.789 --> 00:07:08.539
Speaking of Coal Hill, did you notice how
the similarities in Capaldi’s blackboard

00:07:08.539 --> 00:07:13.139
and all the whiteboards at the school. It’s
like moffat is taunting us with spoilers that

00:07:13.139 --> 00:07:15.960
are just out of focus so we can’t read them
really clearly.

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:19.699
Then there’s clara fiddling with the dalek
innards. That reminded me of 2001 space odyssey.

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:22.020
I’m sorry clara, I can’t let you do that...

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:27.059
Then there was another Doctor mind meld. The
biggest one that comes to mind was the Mr

00:07:27.059 --> 00:07:31.940
Clever mind meld. In addition to the speech
being from Davros’ speech in series 4.

00:07:31.940 --> 00:07:38.180
Feel free to add more references you saw in
the comments.

00:07:38.180 --> 00:07:42.409
Overall I gave the episode a solid A. I enjoyed
this episode more than the premiere. The story

00:07:42.409 --> 00:07:51.379
moved much quicker. It was about half as long,
and 40-42 minutes is perfect.

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:58.830
I love Coal Hill School and Danny Pink is
going to be a lot of fun. I hadn’t seen

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:04.029
any of Samuel Anderson’s previous work but
for me, it’s his sense of humor that really

00:08:04.029 --> 00:08:05.119
does it.

00:08:05.119 --> 00:08:11.659
Doctor Who, in my mind, is all about the balance
of drama and comedy. So you can have your

00:08:11.659 --> 00:08:15.529
crazy dark characters, but they also have
to be funny at the same time. So Danny Pink

00:08:15.529 --> 00:08:19.069
is probably tortured by the people he’s
killed, but he can also bang his head on the

00:08:19.069 --> 00:08:20.069
desk for not asking Clara out.

00:08:20.069 --> 00:08:22.679
If Danny Pink, Clara’s boyfriend slash co-worker
was fun in this episode, I can’t wait to

00:08:22.679 --> 00:08:26.069
see what Danny Pink, Companion, is going to
look like.

00:08:26.069 --> 00:08:28.520
The actual insides of the dalek were amazing
from a visual standpoint. It’s things like

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.499
this that make me totally okay with Moffat
revisting old characters. I’m totally cool

00:08:30.499 --> 00:08:32.870
with it as long as he gives us a perspective
on them we’ve never seen before. Like the

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:36.240
Doctor standing right in front of the Khaled
Mutant.

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:42.669
I feel like the Doctor Ultimately learned
that it was possible for a Dalek to turn good.

00:08:42.669 --> 00:08:47.370
I think we can be very optimistic about Capaldi’s
run. It will be super dark, but the Doctor

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:52.480
will always remain true to his mantra. Never
Cruel, Never Unkind. Always a healer.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:58.190
My favorite quote though, was when Capaldi
said, “I will do something amazing. Promise”.

00:08:58.190 --> 00:09:03.040
The finale is all about broken promises. Which
I’m sure is a clue for Missy.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.240
This is still early in Capaldi’s run so
I feel like we’ll have a much better picture

00:09:06.240 --> 00:09:12.529
of the doctor’s new personality after another
two or three episodes. It took me almost all

00:09:12.529 --> 00:09:14.750
of Series 5 to wrap my brain around Matt Smith.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:23.019
I’m interested to see if the trend continues
and I like Episode 3 robot of sherwood more

00:09:23.019 --> 00:09:27.180
than this episode. I don’t expect that trend
to continue for each episode, but so far I’m

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:29.320
loving the new vibe of the show.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:34.440
Let me know what you thought of all the callbacks
and how you think the Danny Pink Watson vibe

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.670
will play.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:43.259
I will be posting a bonus video next and then
the Q&amp;A video tomorrow. So you guys have a

00:09:43.259 --> 00:09:47.620
ton of time to re-watch the episode and ask
questions. Normally I post bonus videos before

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:53.310
episodes air, but I’m still moving into
a new apartment so my schedule is a little

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.310
weird right now.

00:09:54.310 --> 00:09:58.810
The giveaway for any new people is really
simple. As long as you’re a subscriber you

00:09:58.810 --> 00:10:03.360
can just leave a comment on my doctor who
videos. Then when I post my Q&amp;As I just randomly

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.139
pick someone out and give them an amazon giftcard.
Super simple, it’s open to international

00:10:08.139 --> 00:10:09.139
people too.

00:10:09.139 --> 00:10:13.319
So in case you haven’t seen it yet I’ll
add a link in the description for steven moffat’s

00:10:13.319 --> 00:10:17.730
breakdown of series 8, it has info on all
the episodes. And click here for the Q&amp;A and

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:21.670
here for my Bonus video. I’ll add annotations
for everything as soon as the videos are up.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:24.029
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.
High Fives!

